30,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows our allocation is down nearly a quarter, and the booking system only tracks named slots, leaving unstructured work invisible.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, but the booking system confirms that work without fixed slots simply vanishes from the records.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The staffing picture is grim. Nine ward posts are empty, agency costs are rising, and therapy staff are leaving for the city.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Midori"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Midori: The staffing picture is grim. Nine ward posts are empty, agency costs are rising, and therapy staff are leaving for the city.""}]}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The car park fills before eleven, and the shuttle only reaches four of nineteen villages. We have no physical slack left.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The board minutes show the joint clinic collapsed because neither department would hold the budget line.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that joint clinic failure is a warning. With our budget cut, we cannot afford another program that relies on shared, uncommitted support.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the budget cut is a constraint, but the data proves the model works. We just need to ensure the slots are actually booked.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the model worked, but the staffing review shows therapy staff leaving and midwifery slack. We must match the program to who is actually available.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the staffing slack is useful, but if the car park is full and the shuttle misses most villages, patients simply cannot get to the door.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, access is vital, but the data agreements took fourteen months to sign. We cannot build on promises that take years to secure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, if the booking system only records named slots, how do we guarantee this new program won’t vanish from the reports like the last one?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, we guarantee it by ensuring every single interaction is a named, billable slot. If it isn’t booked, it didn’t happen.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that sounds efficient, but with nine ward posts empty, who actually staffs those slots? We cannot bill for care that no one is there to deliver.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that’s the crux. If the car park is full and the shuttle misses most villages, patients can’t reach the door, so the slots stay empty.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, access is a barrier, but the joint clinic failed because the departments refused to share the rota. We must secure that commitment first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, you are right. We must secure the commitment before spending. I will ensure the ledger reflects a sustainable, single-department model to avoid that collapse.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, a single department is a single point of failure. I want a model that survives if one side withdraws, not one that depends on perfect alignment.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I hear your caution, but with therapy staff leaving and midwifery slack, we must match the program to who is actually available.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I agree on matching staff, but if the car park is full and the shuttle misses most villages, patients can’t reach the door, so the slots stay empty.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, access is a barrier, but the data agreements took fourteen months to sign. We cannot build on promises that take years to secure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
