59,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The candidates are A: Home Follow-Up, B: Day Rehab, C: Perinatal Support, and D: Chronic Care Coordination.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: @Jonathan, Home Follow-Up visits are unstructured. The booking system will erase them, making the program invisible and unfunded.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Shion, Home Follow-Up relies on district nurses, but our ward posts are empty and agency costs are rising. We lack the staff to sustain it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Shion, Home Follow-Up actually solves the access problem. The car park is full, but nurses can reach the villages the shuttle misses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the shared nursing round lost a third of its visits to weather and locked gates. Home visits are fragile, not a solution.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, you are right that unstructured work vanishes. But Home Follow-Up visits can be logged as named slots, ensuring they remain visible and billable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, logging a home visit as a slot is a fiction. The regional fund pays nothing for contacts away from premises. You are proposing a program that earns zero.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that tariff detail is critical. If home visits earn nothing, we cannot fund them. We must look at programs that bill on-site, like Day Rehab or Perinatal Support.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, on-site billing is vital, but Day Rehab needs rooms we don’t have. The car park is full, and the shuttle misses most villages.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the joint clinic failed because departments wouldn’t share the rota. Perinatal Support relies on midwifery and pediatrics. Will they actually commit to the shared schedule?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the staffing review shows midwifery has unusual slack, unlike therapy. If we secure a single, committed rota, Perinatal Support avoids the joint clinic’s collapse.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, slack is not commitment. The board minutes prove departments abandon shared rotas. Perinatal Support is just another joint clinic waiting to collapse.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the slack is real, but the joint clinic failure was about budget ownership, not just staffing. We need a clear single budget line.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Midori"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Midori: @Shion, the slack is real, but the joint clinic failure was about budget ownership, not just staffing. We need a clear single budget line.""}]}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, a single budget line helps, but if the car park is full and the shuttle misses most villages, expectant parents simply cannot reach the door.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, access is a barrier, but the data agreements took fourteen months to sign. We cannot build on promises that take years to secure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, Perinatal Support is internal, so no outside data agreements are needed. We avoid that fourteen-month delay entirely.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, internal is not the same as committed. The board minutes show departments abandoning shared rotas. Perinatal Support is just another joint clinic waiting to collapse.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the midwifery slack is the key. We assign the budget line to midwifery alone, so they own the rota and the money, preventing the shared failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, if midwifery owns it, the car park still fills before eleven. How do we get patients to the door when the shuttle misses most villages?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, the midwifery slack means we can offer evening or weekend slots, avoiding the mid-morning rush. We adapt the schedule to the patients, not the other way around.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
